":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Split rewards teams that control mid and use verticality to their advantage. With Raze, Clove, Gekko, Sage, and Cypher, you’ll dominate site executes, lockdown defense, and clutch retakes. Remember:","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"foreground":"rgb(64, 64, 64)"}}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"qwutj6558","nodes":[],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"BULLETED_LIST","id":"a3u3o431","nodes":[{"type":"LIST_ITEM","id":"566ms432","nodes":[{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"ewp7i433","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Communicate rotations through Vent or ropes!","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"foreground":"rgb(64, 64, 64)"}}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}}]},{"type":"LIST_ITEM","id":"jd8av435","nodes":[{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"gz9ee436","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Save ultimates like Resurrection or Showstopper for critical rounds.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"foreground":"rgb(64, 64, 64)"}}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}}]},{"type":"LIST_ITEM","id":"t4f3z438","nodes":[{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"s0v8n439","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Adapt smokes and traps based on enemy patterns.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"foreground":"rgb(64, 64, 64)"}}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}}]}],"bulletedListData":{"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"sqs4b6682","nodes":[],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"37wv2441","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Ready to climb Split’s ranks? Lock in this comp, master the chaos, and secure the win!","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"foreground":"rgb(64, 64, 64)"}},{"type":"ITALIC","italicData":true}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}}],"documentStyle":{}},"contentText":"Split is one of VALORANT’s most vertical maps, with narrow choke points, multi-level sites, and sneaky flank routes. To master its chaotic lanes, you need agents who can control space, heal allies, and explode onto sites. Below, we break down the best agents for Split  and how to use them in a team comp that dominates both attack and defense. Top Team Composition for Split For aggressive plays and lockdown defense, try this squad: Raze  (Duelist) Clove  (Controller) Gekko  (Initiator) Sage  (Sentinel) Cypher  (Sentinel) Let’s explore why these agents dominate Split: 1. Raze – The Explosive Entry Role : Duelist Why Pick Raze? Blast Pack : Boost into A Tower or B Garage for surprise attacks. Paint Shells : Clear corners like A Screens or B Backsite. Ultimate (Showstopper) : Delete defenders holding tight angles . Pro Tip : Use Boom Bot to scout A Main or B Link before pushing. 2. Clove – The Post-Death Controller Role : Controller Why Pick Clove? Ruse (Smokes) : Block key sightlines like A Heaven or B Tower. Meddle : Decay enemies holding mid Vent or A Ramps. Ultimate (Not Dead Yet) : Revive to retake sites or stall plants. Pro Tip : Smoke mid Mailroom to cut off rotations during executes. 3. Gekko – The Intel Playmaker Role : Initiator Why Pick Gekko? Wingman : Plant/defuse Spike safely on elevated sites. Dizzy : Blind enemies holding A Tower or B Heaven. Ultimate (Thrash) : Clear defenders off high ground (e.g., A Rafters). Pro Tip : Use Mosh Pit to block choke points like B Garage doors. 4. Sage – The Healing Guardian Role : Sentinel Why Pick Sage? Healing Orb : Keep allies alive during mid fights or site pushes. Barrier Orb : Block A Tower stairs or B Main entrances. Ultimate (Resurrection) : Revive a teammate to swing rounds. Pro Tip : Wall off mid Vent to stop fast enemy rotations. 5. Cypher – The Flank Watcher Role : Sentinel Why Pick Cypher? Trapwires : Secure flank routes like B Link or A Sewer. Spycam : Scout A Main or mid Mailroom for early intel. Ultimate (Neural Theft) : Reveal enemy positions after a pick. Pro Tip : Place cages near A Screens to obscure vision during plants. Why This Team Comp Works Aggressive Entry : Raze and Gekko create chaos for easy site takes. Healing + Smokes : Sage and Clove sustain the team while blocking sightlines. Flank Security : Cypher’s traps prevent sneaky backstabs. Map-Specific Tips for Split Attack Strategies A Site Execute : Smoke A Heaven and Ramps, then blast in with Raze’s Paint Shells. Mid Control : Use Sage’s wall to block Vent, then push Mailroom with Gekko’s Dizzy. B Split : Fake B Main, then lurk through B Link with Cypher’s cam. Defense Strategies A Hold : Cypher’s traps in Sewer + Sage’s wall at Tower stairs. B Retake : Clove’s post-death smokes + Raze’s Showstopper clear defenders. Mid Denial : Gekko’s Thrash ult forces enemies out of Vent. Alternative Agents for Split Omen  (Controller): Teleport flanks and smoke key angles. Killjoy  (Sentinel): Lock down sites with turrets and Nanoswarms. Jett  (Duelist): Dash onto sites or Operator angles in mid. Final Thoughts Split rewards teams that control mid and use verticality to their advantage. With Raze, Clove, Gekko, Sage, and Cypher, you’ll dominate site executes, lockdown defense, and clutch retakes. Remember: Communicate rotations through Vent or ropes! Save ultimates like Resurrection or Showstopper for critical rounds. Adapt smokes and traps based on enemy patterns. Ready to climb Split’s ranks? Lock in this comp, master the chaos, and secure the win!"}